OK so both avail arrays are initialized before use. Let me now think about what the actual vulnerability could be.

Wait - I just realized I should look at the `ihevcd_sao_ctb` function more carefully. In that function, `au1_avail_luma` and `au1_avail_chroma` are initialized to 255 UNCONDITIONALLY at the top of the function (lines 170-171). Then they're conditionally set to 0 based on boundary conditions.

In `ihevcd_sao_shift_ctb`, the initialization only happens inside the `else // if(2 <= ...)` blocks. But the boundary condition checks (setting to 0) also happen inside those same blocks. So the initialization and use are properly scoped.

